    "result_text": "Full suite is green (23 tests, 0 failures/errors, BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `membershipNumber` as a server-derived field formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year.\n\nSince `membershipNumber` is derived purely from two fields already on the owner (`customerCode` and `registrationDate`), it fits the existing pattern for the other read-only derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`) rather than needing a persisted column or an `Assign` step. Two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema (example `SMI-0007-M26`), so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression alongside `displayName`/`initials`:\n   ```java\n   String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100)\n   ```\n   The `%02d` zero-pads the two-digit year (e.g. 2007 \u2192 `07`, 2026 \u2192 `26`).\n\nBecause both the create (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) and fetch (`RespondWithOwner`) paths serialize through `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto`, the value appears consistently and is computed at response time \u2014 seed-independent, matching the `Cp14Tests` expectation. All 23 tests pass.",
